# Insatiable Avarice with both modes, the draw mode aimed at Bot2, who answers with Dawn's Truce (hexproof for its player). The spell's only
# target is then illegal as it tries to resolve, so it does not resolve (CR 608.2b) and none of its effects happen - the ruling for spree:
# "If all targets for the chosen modes become illegal before a spell with spree resolves, the spell won't resolve and none of its
# effects will happen". So the other mode's search never happens either: no question is asked and the library keeps its order, the
# Lightning Bolt second. Bot2 draws nothing and loses no life. (Compare the neighbouring scenario where both modes happen in order.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Insatiable Avarice
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Swamp x3
Swamp
Swamp
Lightning Bolt
Swamp x6

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Dawn's Truce
Plains x4
Plains x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Insatiable Avarice.Cast
Bot1.Modes(1; 2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dawn's Truce.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

